This is a utility to acquire information about recently approved applicants
who have passed the New Jersey's Department of Education's background check.
It supports a PTAC effort to bring more volunteers into the buildings.

Really, this is just a proof of concept.  I'm not yet sure where that
information will be stored (and the district is still debating its
volunteer policy which would obviously have a huge impact upon whether
this PTAC effort to bring more volunteers into the schools can even
succeed.  I expect a spreadsheet will be used to store this in the
short term but it evolve eventually into a database (if we choose to
create something fancy like an "applicant portal").

The needed container is started:

  docker compose --ansi never up --build

and then the utility is run:

  docker exec -it background-check-app bin/testGetForDate.0.py --days 10 --county cc --district dddd

to list approvals up to ten days ago where the list is in CSV.  I
believe that this is being used to update a spreadsheet for now.
JSON-generating code remains, and an CLI option could be added to
toggle between formats.



To ease development, this does a little trickery in docker-compose.override.yml.
It mounts volumes containing the source code from the host.  This lets a developer
change and test code w/o rebuilding the container.  The application's Dockerfile
does do the proper COPYing to create a standalone/deployable stack, but I don't
believe I've tested that yet (so some needed components may still be missing).
